1
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:19,560
‎Joseph of Arimathea

2
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:23,439
‎took Jesus Christ down
‎from the cross at Golgotha.

3
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:26,443
‎He cleansed his body and laid him to rest.

4
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:31,156
‎He later became a missionary
‎and set out on a journey.

5
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,408
‎His journey led him to Britannia,

6
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:38,203
‎the northern isle
‎where the British Empire would later rise.

7
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:40,290
‎There, he built a church.

8
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:45,420
‎And there, he drew a map
‎no one could understand.

9
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:48,922
‎No one recognized
‎its coastlines, landforms,

10
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:50,591
‎or where it depicted.

11
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:54,596
‎Joseph himself died
‎without ever explaining it.

12
00:00:57,432 --> 00:01:00,059
‎In 1184,

13
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:04,272
‎a fire broke out at Glastonbury Abbey,
‎built atop the church's ruins.

14
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:08,193
‎A single parchment
‎was found among the ashes.

15
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:14,407
‎It proved to be
‎Joseph of Arimathea's lost map.

16
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:17,993
‎What had Joseph sought?

17
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,828
‎What land did it depict?

18
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:22,373
‎No one ever knew.

19
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:27,002
‎Then, as the 16th century dawned,

20
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:32,509
‎Joseph's map was stolen
‎and disappeared from Glastonbury.

21
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:38,223
‎It happened a couple of years after
‎the discovery of the New World, America.

22
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:40,433
‎And then...

23
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:44,187
‎The year was 1890!

24
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,316
‎What the hell is this?

25
00:01:49,317 --> 00:01:50,943
‎Gyro!

26
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:53,362
‎Wait! Wait up!

27
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:56,615
‎My left hand! What's happening?

28
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:59,202
‎Look!

29
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:08,961
‎What the hell?

30
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:10,712
‎Hey, what's your problem?

31
00:02:10,713 --> 00:02:14,883
‎You call for me,
‎then ignore me and talk to the ground?

32
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:17,469
‎No! There's something there!

33
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:20,305
‎Something just went into my hand!

34
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:23,934
‎It came out of my left hand,
‎then went back in!

35
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:25,562
‎Are you hurt?

36
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:28,022
‎No...

37
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:32,776
‎A hallucination? No, that's not it.

38
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:36,531
‎It's not a hallucination
‎or a Stand ability.

39
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:41,118
‎Making my nails spin at will...

40
00:02:41,119 --> 00:02:43,036
‎That's my Stand ability.

41
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:46,291
‎But my hand... This is different.

42
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,542
‎It feels different.

43
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:50,294
‎There's something in there.

44
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:54,132
‎There's someone else's left hand
‎inside mine!

45
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:57,051
‎But... since when?

46
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:13,818
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

47
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:32,188
‎TUSK, PART 1

48
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:37,567
‎That photo was taken
‎by Balloon No. 3 from 600 feet up.

49
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:41,154
‎523 racers dropped out there.

50
00:04:41,155 --> 00:04:44,241
‎The death toll stands at 68.

51
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:47,119
‎Too many. All from that area?

52
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,287
‎Yes, sir.

53
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:52,499
‎Most appear to have been unhorsed
‎by the quicksand.

54
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,418
‎According to the local Apache,

55
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:59,381
‎this land...
‎They call it the "Devil's Palm."

56
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,049
‎It shifts like quicksand,

57
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:04,304
‎and no one can predict
‎where it'll appear next.

58
00:05:04,887 --> 00:05:08,266
‎The place in the photo disappeared
‎six or seven hours later.

59
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:13,937
‎Geologists believe it's connected
‎to an ancient meteor impact,

60
00:05:13,938 --> 00:05:17,858
‎but why it moves like a living thing
‎remains a mystery.

61
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:21,653
‎The Apache believe that approaching it
‎brings misfortune.

62
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,114
‎They have a saying...

63
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:28,077
‎"The Devil's Palm chooses the people."

64
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:43,050
‎Was Gyro Zeppeli the first
‎to pass through this land?

65
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:46,762
‎Yes, sir. The balloons
‎have lost sight of him.

66
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:49,056
‎But Gyro Zeppeli still leads,

67
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:51,142
‎with Johnny Joestar alongside him.

68
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:55,438
‎They appear to be about 12 miles
‎from the finish at Monument Valley.

69
00:05:56,898 --> 00:06:00,901
‎After Gyro Zeppeli
‎passed through the Devil's Palm...

70
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:04,697
‎Did anyone see him find anything?

71
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:07,658
‎Such as...

72
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:10,995
‎Mr. Steel?

73
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:14,623
‎A corpse, for example.

74
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:19,087
‎It's possible he found a human corpse
‎in this land.

75
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:24,467
‎He may be hiding it
‎in his bags or his tack. Find out.

76
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:29,179
‎Sorry, could you repeat that?

77
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,474
‎I don't mean an entire corpse.

78
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:35,685
‎It could be just a body part,
‎like a hand or a leg.

79
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:38,106
‎It may even be mummified.

80
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:41,526
‎Have the balloons search from the air!

81
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,028
‎This is rather sudden...

82
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:49,616
‎Mr. Steel. Is there another reason
‎you're determined

83
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:51,536
‎to make this race a success?

84
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:55,915
‎Just whose corpse could it be?

85
00:06:56,874 --> 00:06:59,126
‎Let me be perfectly clear.

86
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:03,421
‎We will make the Steel Ball Run a success,
‎no matter what.

87
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:05,133
‎That is our only objective.

88
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:09,929
‎But for now, your only job
‎is to investigate Gyro Zeppeli.

89
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,223
‎Yes, sir.

90
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,059
‎Excuse me.

91
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:24,068
‎Let me correct one thing, Mr. Steel.

92
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,154
‎It's not just "possible."

93
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:29,531
‎Gyro Zeppeli has found it.

94
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:31,575
‎At the Devil's Palm.

95
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:34,327
‎I'm 100% certain.

96
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:36,831
‎Gyro Zeppeli found the corpse.

97
00:07:38,499 --> 00:07:44,421
‎The man we sent, Oye,
‎left a message at the checkpoint.

98
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:48,800
‎Unfortunately, he was defeated
‎before he could take the corpse.

99
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:53,306
‎So Gyro Zeppeli's after the corpse,
‎just like we are?

100
00:07:55,224 --> 00:07:57,934
‎We don't know yet.

101
00:07:57,935 --> 00:08:01,813
‎He may have found it by chance
‎during the race.

102
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:05,817
‎Or he may not even realize
‎he's found it yet.

103
00:08:05,818 --> 00:08:10,281
‎That's the nature of the corpse
‎and the Devil's Palm.

104
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:13,159
‎The corpse chooses the person!

105
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:17,412
‎The important thing here

106
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:20,790
‎is that the corpse won't disappear
‎after Gyro is eliminated.

107
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:27,215
‎To do that, we must determine
‎how and where he's carrying it.

108
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,927
‎Wait a minute! Eliminate Gyro Zeppeli?

109
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:34,596
‎I agreed to cooperate fully,

110
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:38,433
‎but no one said
‎there'd be murder in my race!

111
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:40,268
‎I thought we were
‎just looking for the corpse!

112
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:41,854
‎Listen carefully, Mr. Steel.

113
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:45,774
‎Obtaining that corpse is justice!

114
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,818
‎We'll use whatever means are necessary!

115
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:52,155
‎Humanity has long sought that corpse
‎more than any power

116
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:54,367
‎or treasure in history.

117
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:59,121
‎In the end, we'll have it for sure!

118
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:11,509
‎Make the Steel Ball Run a success.

119
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:14,971
‎A race that follows the route
‎marked on this map.

120
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:18,974
‎If someone with the ability
‎follows this route,

121
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:21,811
‎they will surely
‎gather the scattered corpse parts.

122
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:26,690
‎And then... "Murder"?

123
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:29,026
‎Choose your words carefully, Steven Steel.

124
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:34,865
‎Without me, this race
‎would never have happened.

125
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:40,997
‎Understood.

126
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:43,499
‎President...

127
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:45,835
‎of the United States.

128
00:09:49,213 --> 00:09:50,839
‎Excuse me. I brought coffee.

129
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,843
‎Don't come in!
‎You're not cleared to enter!

130
00:09:59,932 --> 00:10:01,600
‎Mr. President!

131
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:04,144
‎My deepest apologies. This is my wife.

132
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:05,813
‎She doesn't know any better...

133
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,111
‎Be careful.

134
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:15,822
‎Yes, sir! My sincerest apologies...

135
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,407
‎Not me.

136
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:21,202
‎Your young, beautiful wife.

137
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:22,413
‎Above her head.

138
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:37,927
‎What my men carry out,

139
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:39,096
‎Mr. Steel,

140
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,848
‎is an operation.

141
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:43,683
‎Not murder.

142
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:46,812
‎Not when they act on my orders!

143
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:53,486
‎On the roof...

144
00:10:54,570 --> 00:10:56,447
‎Is that a person?

145
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:58,949
‎How is that possible?

146
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:01,243
‎It spilled...

147
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:03,162
‎but nothing's wet.

148
00:11:04,038 --> 00:11:05,247
‎Where's the coffee?

149
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:13,213
‎Hey, Johnny.
‎Have you ever been to an opera?

150
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:14,714
‎An opera.

151
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:17,050
‎An opera? That music thing?

152
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:20,011
‎The kind of play
‎where they could just say the lines,

153
00:11:20,012 --> 00:11:23,515
‎but suddenly start singing
‎to explain the situation instead?

154
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:24,558
‎What else?

155
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:27,769
‎No, but why do you ask?

156
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,396
‎Just curious.

157
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:32,607
‎They're called opera glasses
‎because they're for opera, right?

158
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:35,777
‎But those singers on the stage...

159
00:11:35,778 --> 00:11:37,695
‎They're huge, aren't they?

160
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:40,698
‎That's probably
‎why they've got such powerful voices.

161
00:11:40,699 --> 00:11:44,327
‎So why use opera glasses to look at them?

162
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:47,206
‎You don't need opera glasses.
‎The singers are huge.

163
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:54,170
‎What, to see if the buttons
‎on their fancy costumes are about to pop?

164
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:56,424
‎True. You've got a point.

165
00:11:56,924 --> 00:12:02,221
‎Or because they all have the same build,
‎you have to get a closer look?

166
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:06,058
‎Johnny! That's a good one!

167
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:11,354
‎Look, Gyro. That's Monument Valley.

168
00:12:11,355 --> 00:12:13,440
‎We're an hour or two from the finish.

169
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,108
‎Should we pick up the pace?

170
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,360
‎No. We'll keep this pace.

171
00:12:17,361 --> 00:12:19,280
‎We can still take first.

172
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:50,186
‎Gyro?

173
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:03,616
‎Gyro! Where are you?

174
00:13:04,366 --> 00:13:05,367
‎Gyro!

175
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:13,042
‎Did he fall off his horse?

176
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:14,752
‎No way!

177
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:17,795
‎Gyro! Answer me!

178
00:13:17,796 --> 00:13:20,798
‎Where are you, Gyro?

179
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:21,800
‎Gyro!

180
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,428
‎Gyro!

181
00:13:27,014 --> 00:13:28,057
‎Gyro!

182
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:37,524
‎An enemy... We're under attack.

183
00:13:37,525 --> 00:13:40,903
‎His horse...
‎Only Gyro's horse disappeared.

184
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:42,905
‎But how?

185
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:45,491
‎Gyro!

186
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:48,994
‎Where are you, Gyro?

187
00:13:49,703 --> 00:13:51,330
‎Answer me!

188
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:04,677
‎What is this? Even his gear is gone!

189
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:08,472
‎It's all disappearing!

190
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:12,184
‎What?

191
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:17,731
‎The enemy's above us!
‎Somehow, it's overhead!

192
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:23,403
‎What kind of power is this?

193
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:25,698
‎What's up there?

194
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:41,463
‎It's a Stand User!

195
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,384
‎I'm a target too!

196
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:49,220
‎Gyro isn't their only target.

197
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:51,222
‎Just as I thought,

198
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:54,101
‎this race was never
‎just about winning or losing!

199
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,610
‎My horse too!

200
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:05,279
‎Damn it! How's that possible?

201
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:08,115
‎Where is it? What's there?

202
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,881
‎What's this?

203
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:27,176
‎The feather... It's coming from inside!

204
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:33,265
‎I can't cut it!

205
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:45,861
‎A Stand ability!

206
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:50,115
‎So that feather connects to another space?

207
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:54,995
‎Gyro and his horse
‎were snagged by those hooks...

208
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:05,505
‎They're after me!

209
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:08,217
‎They're trying to snag me!

210
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:12,471
‎It's hollow under that rock. That'll work!

211
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:16,892
‎Anyway, I've got to hide under there!

212
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:14,699
‎It's above me. Right above me.

213
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:17,828
‎This enemy is determined to kill me.

214
00:17:18,704 --> 00:17:21,039
‎But what would that accomplish?

215
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:25,168
‎If they wanted me out of the race,
‎it's as good as done.

216
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:27,378
‎My horse, my saddle...
‎everything's gone.

217
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:29,339
‎Gyro's gear and horse too.

218
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:33,302
‎Are they looking for

219
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,595
‎something?

220
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:39,348
‎They went after Gyro first,
‎then my horse and gear...

221
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:42,728
‎And now they won't stop coming after me.

222
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:47,691
‎Because they think we're hiding something.

223
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:51,570
‎Then what are they looking for?

224
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,324
‎The thing that could be valuable is...

225
00:17:58,952 --> 00:18:02,288
‎They ignored Gyro's Steel Ball.

226
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:04,541
‎I don't have anything but my horse...

227
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:11,048
‎No way... Could it be
‎that mummified left arm I saw?

228
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,884
‎So it wasn't a hallucination.

229
00:18:14,426 --> 00:18:17,678
‎Oye... Stroheim too...

230
00:18:17,679 --> 00:18:22,768
‎Not just them. The terrorists
‎are all after the arm inside my hand!

231
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:26,145
‎What is that mummified arm?

232
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:28,816
‎Just whose arm is it?

233
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:50,170
‎Whir, whir, whir...

234
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:56,760
‎Ka-plunk!

235
00:18:57,511 --> 00:19:01,223
‎Creak... Ka-plunk!

236
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:04,935
‎Grab.

237
00:19:07,563 --> 00:19:08,564
‎Huh?

238
00:19:14,653 --> 00:19:15,779
‎Sniff, sniff, sniff...

239
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:20,534
‎Pop! Slurp, slurp, slurp...

240
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:22,493
‎That's good!

241
00:19:22,494 --> 00:19:24,203
‎Creak... Ka-plunk!

242
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:26,247
‎But it's not here.

243
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:28,791
‎It's not in this gear either!

244
00:19:28,792 --> 00:19:30,459
‎So that means...

245
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:33,713
‎Johnee... What was his name again?

246
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:35,214
‎Joshter.

247
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:37,341
‎Johnee Joshter.

248
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:40,052
‎He's carrying it himself.

249
00:19:40,053 --> 00:19:44,015
‎That settles it!
‎He's got it hidden somewhere on him!

250
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:46,768
‎Ka-plunk! Creak... Ka-plunk!

251
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,248
‎No way...

252
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:11,209
‎Gyro, where are you?

253
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:13,253
‎Are you alive? Or are you dead?

254
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:18,592
‎I only wanted to learn
‎the secret of your Steel Ball.

255
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:22,136
‎Ever since that strange arm
‎attached itself to me.

256
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:25,265
‎Damn it!
‎If I leave this place, they'll kill me.

257
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:28,142
‎Gyro, help me.

258
00:20:28,143 --> 00:20:29,728
‎What am I supposed to do?

259
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:36,025
‎No vacancy here.

260
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:38,904
‎We're fully booked for months!

261
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:48,455
‎What the...

262
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,040
‎It's not just the feather!

263
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:53,585
‎This ability is a lure!

264
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:58,131
‎I've got to get the hook out!

265
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:00,008
‎Hurry...

266
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:04,429
‎What?

267
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:16,608
‎I'm done for!

268
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:21,697
‎They're going to kill me.
‎Once they realized it's inside me...

269
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:23,740
‎Then...

270
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:25,783
‎You can have it!

271
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:28,452
‎If you want it that badly,
‎you can have it!

272
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:30,871
‎It's not like I wanted it
‎in the first place!

273
00:21:30,872 --> 00:21:33,249
‎I don't need this thing!

274
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:35,168
‎Just take it!

275
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:57,774
‎Movēre crūs.

276
00:21:58,483 --> 00:21:59,484
‎What the...

277
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:35,956
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
